  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A mass on the end of a string is rotating on a frictionless table in circular motion of radius R<sub>1</sub> and undergoes an angular displacement of θ in time t.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The string tension is kept constant, but the angular displacement of the mass is increased to 2θ in time t. The radius of the motion changes to R<sub>2</sub>.</p>\n<p>What is R<sub>2</sub>?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R_{1}}{4}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\">2R<sub>1</sub></li><li data-label=\"C\">4R<sub>1</sub></li><li data-label=\"D\">R<sub>1</sub> × R<sub>1</sub></li></ol>"
  },
